  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated multi-sectoral emergency response to reduce morbidity and mortality by ensuring access to healthcare, including advanced nutrition services, targeting the most vulnerable populations in prioritized sub-districts of Syria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed Project targets 11 sub-districts as part of a multi-sectoral approach to responding to health emergencies complicated by malnutrition. It aims to reduce morbidity and mortality by restoring access to healthcare, including essential nutrition actions. The WHO project complements the UNICEF response in the allocation and targets 296,266 affected people with activities in the Health sector.</narrative>
  </description>
